---
import {officialCourseUrl} from '../lib/official-practice';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import ResourceLibrary from '../components/ResourceLibrary';import {sources} from '../lib/catalog';
---
<Layout title="Resources" active="Resources"><div class="page-top"><h1>Study resources</h1><p>Official event guides, sample tests, and the references used in these lessons. Check the current rules first, then choose any extra reading you need.</p></div><section class="stage-panel" style="margin-bottom:30px;max-width:850px"><h2>Official FBLA practice tests</h2><p>Open your event’s practice section for a direct link to its official sample test, or browse FBLA’s high-school practice course. Sign in with your own CONNECT member account. Sample role plays and production tasks are in preparation resources.</p><p><a href={officialCourseUrl} class="button button-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open FBLA’s official practice course ↗</a></p><a href="https://support.fbla.org/hc/en-us/articles/4416902542996-Competition-Prep-Sample-Objective-Tests-Role-Plays-Production-Tests-and-Case-Competitions" class="plain-link" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">FBLA’s access instructions ↗</a></section><section class="archive-directory-intro"><h2>Google Drive study archive</h2><p>Browse all 274 files by event and material type. Files with the same title are grouped together. Older rules are labeled historical.</p><a href="/resources/archive/" class="plain-link">Browse the Drive archive →</a></section><ResourceLibrary client:load sources={sources}/><section class="prose" style="margin-top:45px"><h2>How we use these sources</h2><p>The lessons and lesson checks were written for this site. Event practice tests link to FBLA’s own CONNECT course. Current Maryland guides set district requirements; national guides set NLC requirements. Public educational resources help explain the concepts. Sources can change, so check the official guide before submitting work.</p><p>Historical Drive materials are optional practice references. They include duplicates and older event names, and their accuracy and reuse rights have not been established. We link to originals rather than republishing that collection.</p><p>A sample test may not cover everything in your event. If requirements conflict, compare the original documents and ask your adviser.</p></section></Layout>

